quran[26]{c,v,t}:
  56,51,"Then, indeed, you, O straying deniers,"
  56,52,shall eat from the (bitter thorny) tree of Zaqqum.
  56,53,"And you will fill (your) bellies with it,"
  56,54,"and drink boiling water over it,"
  56,55,drinking (it) like thirsty camels.’
  56,56,This shall be the welcome feast they receive on the Day of Resurrection.
  56,57,It is We Who created you. Then why do you not acknowledge it?
  56,58,Have you considered (the sperm) you ejaculate (into the womb)?
  56,59,"Are you creating (a child from) it, or are We the Creators?"
  56,60,"We have decreed death among you, and We cannot be stopped,"
  56,61,from replacing you with your likes and recreating you in (a way) that you do not know.
  56,62,You indeed know the first genesis. Then why are you not mindful (of guidance)?
  56,63,Have you considered what you sow?
  56,64,"Are you causing it to grow, or are We the Growers?"
  56,65,"Had We willed, We would have reduced this (harvest) to trash, and you would have been left astoundingly regretful,"
  56,66,"(saying to yourself:) ‘Indeed, We have suffered a (great) loss."
  56,67,"Rather, we are deprived (of our livelihood).’"
  56,68,Have you considered the water you drink?
  56,69,"Do you bring it down from the clouds, or are We the Ones Who bring (it) down?"
  56,70,"Had We willed, We would have made it bitter. Why do you not give thanks?"
  56,71,Have you considered the fire that you kindle?
  56,72,"Are you who brought its tree into being, or are We the Creator?"
  56,73,We have made it (i.e. the fire) a reminder (of the Hell) and (the trees) a (source of) provision for the desert dwellers.
  56,74,"So glorify the Name of your Lord, the All-Magnificent."
  56,75,So I swear by the positions of the stars.*
  56,76,"Indeed, it is a magnificent oath if you could know."
